.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt PANELTEST 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm paneltest
.Nd step the PicoCalc panel controller through register sets
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens
.Pa /dev/lcdgfx ,
reads the ST7365P panel controller's registers back through
.Va machdep.picocalc.panel_read ,
measures the frame rate through
.Va machdep.picocalc.panel_scan ,
and draws calibration patterns while
.Va machdep.picocalc.panel_variant
selects one of the register sets compiled into a kernel built with
.Dv LCD_PANELTEST .
Other kernels refuse both variables and
.Nm
then shows the patterns under the shipped settings only.
It needs the superuser.
The top left corner of every pattern shows the set number, its name,
the pattern number and the rate measured under the set.
.Pp
Keys:
.Bl -tag -width "right, left" -compact
.It Cm right , left , n , p , d , a
next or previous register set
.It Cm down , up , s , w
next or previous pattern
.It Cm 1 Ns - Ns Cm 7
pattern: text and readback, black and white edges, gray bars,
subpixel columns, 50% gray flicker, crosstalk square, scroll lines
.It Cm r
read the registers back and show them raw and decoded
.It Cm f
sample the controller's scanline, then log, print and show the
frame rate with its error bound and the line count
.It Cm q
quit; closing the device programs the shipped set again
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/log/paneltest.log" -compact
.It Pa /var/log/paneltest.log
every set change, readback and frame-rate measurement, appended
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sysctl 8
